@@ -15,3 +15,47 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Accounts and passkeys
+
+Sign in at `/devtools-times/signin`, create an account at `/devtools-times/signup`,
+and manage passkeys at `/devtools-times/account/settings`. Both password and
+password-free account creation are supported. Passkeys are registered and verified
+on the server with SimpleWebAuthn, require user verification, and use discoverable
+credentials for username-free sign-in. The client never stores authentication tokens.
+
+Account settings support adding, naming, renaming, and removing passkeys. Sensitive
+changes require authentication within the last five minutes; otherwise the UI asks
+for a passkey or the account's existing password. An account without a password
+cannot remove its last passkey. Removal revokes the server credential; the user
+must separately remove its copy from their password manager.
+
+These routes replace the previous remote demo password API with a local account
+store. Existing accounts in that remote service are **not migrated**. New accounts
+are persisted in `.data/auth.json`, excluded from Git. The store contains salted
+scrypt password hashes, public credential material, hashed opaque session tokens,
+and short-lived, single-use challenges. Cookies are HTTP-only and SameSite Strict;
+HTTPS enables Secure cookies. Passkeys require HTTPS, except on localhost.
+
+Configuration:
+
+- `AUTH_ORIGIN`: the exact public origin (e.g. `https://example.com`), without the
+  application path. Set this explicitly behind a reverse proxy. It controls origin
+  verification and the relying party hostname. Keep the hostname stable: passkeys
+  are bound to it. Defaults to the incoming request origin for local development.
+- `AUTH_DATA_FILE`: path to the account store; defaults to `.data/auth.json`.
+  Use a persistent volume for deployments. The serialized file store is intended
+  for this single-process demo. A deployment with multiple workers or replicas
+  needs a shared transactional database and shared rate limiting.
+
+Validation without starting a server:
+
+```sh
+pnpm test
+pnpm run build
+```
+
+The tests cover password hashing, secret-free account responses, serialized writes,
+and expiration cleanup. They do not exercise a real authenticator. See the
+[SimpleWebAuthn documentation](https://simplewebauthn.dev/docs/packages/server/)
+for the WebAuthn verification library used here.
